the enduring popularity of the witcher  books and games means that long-time  fans of the franchise have strong  opinions many feel protective over these  characters since they have lived with  them longer than the netflix show has  existed geralt himself is one of the  things that fans are most protective of  for season 2 actor henry cavill  requested one change in regards to how  geralt should be portrayed specifically  that he'd be a bit more vocal and this  is for the best as far as die hard fans  are concerned as it makes him closer to  how he's portrayed in the books season 2  has received a better reception than the  first which was criticized by many over  its confusing use of multiple timelines  so it's clear that the creators of the  show were listening it took me to the  fourth verse to understand their  different timelines  that magic kiss that was a bit cheap  still even though the show is clearly  improving as it goes along it doesn't  mean fans don't have their gripes with  how season 2 adapts the beloved source  material it's based on there is one  season 2 scene in particular that fans  have not exactly appreciated one of the  running threads in the witcher is  geralt's horse roach roach is a constant  companion to geralt but it is not always  the same horse geralt has had many  roaches during his long life but has  loved every one of them that is what  makes it so devastating when the  audience is forced to watch roach be  killed in season 2 episode 6. while on  the road geralt and siri encounter the  deadly monolith beast that was briefly  glimpsed earlier being a witcher geralt  is able to successfully keep the monster  at bay unfortunately roach is just an  elderly horse and gets caught in a  crossfire this doesn't end well for the  poor animal who dies a bloody death in  the aftermath of the battle the scene of  geralt being forced to say goodbye to  his faithful friend caused a bit of an  uproar in reddit one user posted  obviously we all know giving geralt's  age that he's had multiple roaches we  also know he'll have more in the future  knowing that and seeing roach lying on  the ground ripped to shreds two entirely  different things  some fans were just heartbroken with one  user admitting i haven't felt this gut  wrench since hedwig died on twitter one  fan posted they didn't have to show us  roach's entire death scene but i guess  they decided it was worth it  while another shared pride over roach's  death it's true in all fairness the  witcher treats roach's death as a pretty  massive story beat and the horse's  demise receives the same attention as  most human deaths in the show do if not  more however this doesn't remove the  salt from the wound the brutal death of  roach is not something that occurs in  the source material and even worse  geralt ends up being the one who  ultimately has to put roach out of his  misery though such events may well have  occurred during the witcher's long life  before even he's somewhat shaken by the  incident as such it's easy to understand  that this is a moment that many fans  simply could not get behind nevertheless  the people behind the show already knew  that the show's roach was getting older  than a horse can believably be and must  die at some point in any case as such  they were adamant that geralt's poor  steed gets ascending off it receives  showrunner lauren schmidt his rick told  gamesradar in terms of how we killed off  roach i thought if we're going to do  this i want to make it a part of the  story i don't want roach to die off  screen and no one ever mentions it being  the witcher expert that he is henry  cavill personally wrote the little  eulogy geralt gives to say goodbye to  roach  enjoy your close walk across the meadow  and through the mist  historic told gamesradar when we kill  roach on screen henry actually wrote  what he says to the horse it was wildly  emotional it really felt like saying  goodbye to a character we wanted to make  sure that we honored it in the right way  and that we made his death heroic the  witcher season 2 is available for  streaming on netflix  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the witcher are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

